Description: Supervised multi-omics integration for block-missing
    ("ragged") data, where some subjects lack one or more whole omics
    modalities (assay blocks) rather than scattered individual values. WOVEN
    fits a shared latent space with SUMCOR (sum of correlations) multi-set
    canonical correlation analysis, a criterion that maximizes the summed
    pairwise correlation between modalities' latent scores, using only the
    anchor subjects observed in every modality; class labels enter through a
    label-augmented cross-covariance, and per-modality graph Laplacians
    regularize the fit. Every other subject is then scored from the
    modalities it has by a Nystrom extension, a way to place new points in an
    already fitted embedding (for WOVEN's linear embedding, multiplying the
    observed features by the learned projection matrices), so no missing
    block is imputed. The effective sample size (ESS) retention, the fraction
    of subjects a method can score, is therefore the fraction with at least
    one observed modality, rather than the complete-case fraction.
    woven_tune() chooses the regularization settings by cross-validated
    balanced error rate, and the fitted model is summarized by plots and a
    table of the top features per modality.
